            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ms. Sarah E. Harrington, Charles Glover (the respondent) argues that the assumption that an unlicensed owner is the driver is not justified because the officer had no knowledge of who was driving."
      }
    ],
