          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0001-0012"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 36,
                "start": 36
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Sarah E. Harrington, Glover\u2019s counsel argues that the Court has been asked to adopt a nationwide bright\u2011line rule that it is always reasonable to assume an unlicensed owner is driving, but no evidence has been provided to support that assumption."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Sarah E. Harrington",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0001-0013"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 37,
                "start": 37
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Sarah E. Harrington, the respondent points out that the officer stipulated he had no idea who was driving and declined to testify about why an unlicensed driver would be presumed to be behind the wheel."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Sarah E. Harrington",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0001-0015"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 39,
                "start": 39
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Sarah E. Harrington, the core question, according to the respondent, is whether an owner who lacks a valid license usually drives the vehicle, not merely whether owners typically drive their cars."
        }
      ],
